{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792406847,"nonce":"P3YS05dTWD3ExmsSWsZyc9vVNns=","title":"A window with only idle animations spins the loop at 100% CPU and floods the heap with garbage","message":"**Symptom**\nNatively on macOS the dashboard (apps/dashboard/run.sh) went unresponsive: the pointer spun, Activity Monitor said \"ash (Not Responding)\", CPU sat at 100% with the window idle, and the footprint reached 1.2-1.3 GB on a page with nothing moving.\n\n**Cause**\nWindowedApp's loop sleeps in window.wait(timeout) between turns: 50 ms when the animation tickers changed nothing drawn, else 1/120 s. Work.notify() called the host's wake even from the loop's own thread in its own turn, and the dashboard's Model ticker writes signals every turn, so a wake was always pending and wait returned at once. Idle pages ran about 57,000 turns a second, each allocating about 3 KB (about 180-300 MB/s of garbage), so the collector and the footprint grew without a frame being drawn.\n\nFrames hid it before: the island's equalizer canvas read the model clock unconditionally, so every page redrew on every frame and vsync paced the loop.\n\n**Reproducer**\nA scratch driver that opens the dashboard on More, with ASHUI_FRAME_STATS=1: loop turns per second from a ticker counter, and hl.Gc.stats().totalAllocated. Before: about 57,000 turns/s and 180 MB/s. After: 20 turns/s and under 1 MB/s.\n\n**Fix**\nWork.notify on the loop's own thread during a turn marks late work instead of waking; WindowedApp.loop asks Work.end() before it sleeps, and takes the writes a tick made at its flush (Work.settle). A turn that drew a frame does not sleep (vsync paces it); one that drew nothing sleeps its full step.\n\nThe island equalizer and the media visualiser read the clock only while a track plays, so a paused page draws nothing.\n\n**Memory**\nThe collector's next trigger sat at 512 MB with live data near 140 MB, and idle collection does not run while the loop wakes every 50 ms, so garbage floated until the threshold. Memory.collectSoon (haxe/ashui/core/Memory.hx) collects once, 1.5 s after the dashboard's page changes: a major collection takes 4-25 ms and returns about 100-300 MB. On the idle More page after visiting every page the footprint is about 500 MB (Ash heap 150, native allocations 230, GPU 120); a fresh More page is about 330 MB.\n\n**Left**\nNative and GPU memory held after leaving the car pages (model textures, retained map canvases) is not released with the page. Navigate allocates about 80 MB/s while it animates (route canvas redrawn every frame).","files":null}]}